    {
      "id": "40",
      "type": "writeup",
      "attributes": {
        "id": 40,
        "body_ja": "",
        "body": "<p>In Japanese, almost any type of word can be attached to the beginning of a noun to modify the meaning, or describe the qualities of that noun. However, depending on the type of word used, conjugation rules will differ slightly.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>For <span data-gp-id='28'>な-Adjectives</span>, they will always need to be followed by <span data-gp-id='28'>な</span>, when used before a noun. This means that adjective (A) is describing qualities/features of noun (B).</p>\r\n\r\n<ul class='writeup-examples--holder'>\r\n<li data-study-question='154835'>\r\n<li data-study-question='154836'></ul>\r\n\r\n<section class='caution'><h4>Caution</h4>\r\n<p>Many words can take either <span data-gp-id='28'>な</span> or <span data-gp-id='6'>の</span> when describing a noun. The difference in meaning is usually clear. Let's take a look at both nuances.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>(A) <span data-gp-id='28'>な</span> (B) means that - (A) is a quality/feature of (B)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>(A) <span data-gp-id='6'>の</span> (B) means that - (A) is the type/purpose of (B)</p>\r\n\r\n<ul class='writeup-examples--holder'>\r\n<li data-study-question='183766'>\r\n<li data-study-question='183767'></ul>\r\n\r\n<p>To avoid making this mistake when using <span data-gp-id='28'>な-Adjectives</span> to describe a noun, it can be helpful to think about whether you are describing a 'quality', or the 'purpose' of something.</p></section>"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "1341",
      "type": "related_content",
      "attributes": {
        "id": 1341,
        "relationship_type": "misc",
        "body": "な-Adjectives describe nouns and connect to them using な (e.g., 好きな本 = 'a book I like'). の also connects nouns, with the first noun describing the second (e.g., 日本人の学生 = 'a Japanese student'). The choice between な and の depends on the type of word, though some words can function as both な-Adjectives or nouns with different nuances (e.g., 幸せな日 vs. 幸せの理由).",
        "first_relatable": {
          "id": 954,
          "slug": "な-adjective-noun",
          "title": "な-Adjective + Noun",
          "meaning": "Describing a noun",
          "level": "JLPT5",
          "type_pascal": "GrammarPoint",
          "type_snake": "grammar_point"
        },
        "second_relatable": {
