          "slug": "の",
          "title": "の",
          "meaning": "Indicates possession",
          "level": "JLPT5",
          "type_pascal": "GrammarPoint",
          "type_snake": "grammar_point"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "1340",
      "type": "related_content",
      "attributes": {
        "id": 1340,
        "relationship_type": "related",
        "body": "い-Adjectives connect directly to nouns (e.g., 面白い本) and aren't followed by だ in plain form (e.g., この本は面白い). な-Adjectives, on the other hand, connect to nouns using な (e.g., 好きな本) and are followed by だ in plain form (e.g., この本は好きだ). Note that not all adjectives ending in い are い-Adjectives (e.g., 綺麗, written as きれい in hiragana, is a な-Adjective, e.g., きれいな月).",
        "first_relatable": {
